.\" crash-command: pte
.\" crash-symbol: help_pte
.TH CRASH-PTE 8
.SH NAME
crash-pte \- translate a page table entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pte
contents ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This command translates the hexadecimal contents of a PTE into its physical
page address and page bit settings.  If the PTE references a swap location,
the swap device and offset are displayed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
    crash> pte d8e067
.fi
.PP
.B PTE    PHYSICAL  FLAGS
.nf
    d8e067   d8e000   (PRESENT|RW|USER|ACCESSED|DIRTY)

    crash> pte 13f600
.fi
.PP
.B PTE      SWAP     OFFSET
.nf
    13f600  /dev/hda2   5104
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crash (8)
